# RobuNexa NAM Reanimate

## Migration build

- Hosted built-in moveset, dance, limb-map and hat-map modules in RobuNexa.
- Pinned the main entry point and built-in module snapshot to immutable commit revisions.
- Removed the legacy Pusher listener that compiled and executed remote event text.
- Removed unrelated third-party MP3 downloads from startup checks.
- Added 15 original R6 anime-inspired animation sequences and a NAM Dances module.
- Added a GitHub loadstring launcher and detailed Turkish/English migration documentation.
- Left the community marketplace empty until modules can be reviewed and licensed.

## Verification status

- Verified the encoded animation payloads decode to valid-looking little-endian KeyframeSequence records with sorted keyframes and expected animation names.
- Not tested in a live Roblox executor or a live game. Pose quality, executor compatibility, and limb-reanimation behavior still need runtime testing.

See README.md and NAM-ROBUNEXA-MIGRATION.md for setup, limitations and safety notes.

- Added native binary Hakari dance .anim from the upstream Uhhhhhh content repository with attribution.
- Documented public Gojo/Sukuna/Kira Creator Store listings separately; did not rehost those marketplace assets.
